            <ArticleTitle>Disseminated Herpes Zoster with Meningo-encephalitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>256-257</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 65 year old, immunocompetent, male patient developed herpes zoster ophthalmicus associated with a generalized varicellifform euption and meningo-encephalitis. Meningo-encephalitis was diagnosed on the basis of CSF picture. The patient responded in seven clays to oral acyclovir (400 mg five times a day).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
